ipment in Caldria, so its plan carries the most weight.\n- **Norvane Utilities:** it plans a 12% increase in 2027 capital spending, also mostly on substations and transformers.\n\nThis rests on two documents from the search. One is a short note on the 2027 capital plans. The other is the Q3 2026 credit conditions note. I found no order backlog, delivery or pricing data, so this shows planned spending, not confirmed orders.\n\n**Financing risk:** the credit note suggests the plans can probably be funded, but not without friction.\n- **Debt:** utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably.\n- **Equity:** two utility share offerings were cut back in size.\n\nIf funding tightens, some of the planned spending could slip. I'd treat that as a risk to the timing of the increase, not a reason to doubt its direction. Whether the utilities can finance the plans is a separate question that n3's nodes (n7 for debt markets, n8 for equity markets) are working on. Data-centre demand is also separate, and n6 is covering it.","ttft_ms":4032,"type":"result","duration_ms":16448,"uuid":"d96914cf-64f9-4314-851c-7ae4ac064e27","ttft_stream_ms":3108,"time_to_request_ms":64,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":3,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":14,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":61,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":206,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":132,"process_rss_mib_result":205,"process_anon_mib_result":124,"process_peak_rss_mib":225,"pro